      {
        "block_id": "LgiKdaCRNoFibOxWgyYcGknhncU",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "V9Bfd5rgAoqvqbxgIQwcyEGTn6d",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "When implementing a ColBERT-like text retrieval system in Milvus, you are not limited to splitting documents into tokens. ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "A9zPdkvIRo1b6dxTb3PcC9r6ncb",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "V9Bfd5rgAoqvqbxgIQwcyEGTn6d",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Instead, you can divide the documents into segments of any appropriate size, embed each segment to create an embedding list, and store the document along with its embedded segments in an entity.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "XDC5dUqtxoAmkXx4blxcQ0Asnlc",
        "block_type": 5,
        "heading3": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "ColPali extension",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        },
        "parent_id": "I59YdqMpioEHGVxFiqccJawsnZf"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "RU8bdJeTQoAqg5xCMB6c04Dqnne",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "I59YdqMpioEHGVxFiqccJawsnZf",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Based on ColBERT, ColPali (arXiv: ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "2407.01449",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "link": {
                    "url": "https%3A%2F%2Farxiv.org%2Fabs%2F2407.01449%3Fspm%3Da2ty_o01.29997173.0.0.31c4c9217HFv28%26file%3D2407.01449"
                  },
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": ") proposes a novel approach to visually rich document retrieval that leverages Vision-Language Models (VLMs). During data ingestion, each document page is rendered into a high-resolution image, then split into patches, rather than tokenized. For example, a document page image of 448 x 448 pixels can produce 1,024 patches, each measuring 14 x 14 pixels.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "MxMrdofAkomQfNxAQflcY1F6n3e",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "I59YdqMpioEHGVxFiqccJawsnZf",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "This method preserves non-textual information, such as the document layout, images, and table structures, which are lost when using text-only retrieval systems.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "ExfadzUvzoizu2xUXR1czghVnfe",
        "block_type": 43,
        "board": {
          "token": "SuHjwmWiDhLs79buw22cw9aAnqf"
        },
        "parent_id": "I59YdqMpioEHGVxFiqccJawsnZf"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "LeoudahcwogHMZxtWQgcQvfJnmh",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "I59YdqMpioEHGVxFiqccJawsnZf",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "The VLM used in ColPali is called PaliGemma (arXiv: ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "2407.07726",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "link": {
                    "url": "https%3A%2F%2Farxiv.org%2Fhtml%2F2407.07726v2%23S1"
                  },
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "), which comprises an image encoder (",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "SigLIP-400M",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "), a decoder-only language model (",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Gemma2-2B",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "), and a linear layer that projects the image encoder's output into the language model's vector space, as shown in the above diagram.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "MGBid4C78ofenyxBfIbcjg2Cncb",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "I59YdqMpioEHGVxFiqccJawsnZf",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "During data ingestion, a document page, represented as a raw image, is divided into multiple visual patches, each of which is embedded to generate a list of vector embeddings. Then they are projected into the language model's vector space to obtain the final embedding list, as in ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "equation": {
                "content": "d \\rightarrow E_d = [e_{d1}, e_{d2}, \\dots, e_{dn}] ∈ \\R^{n×d}\n",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": ". When a query arrives, it is tokenized, and each token is embedded to generate a list of vector embeddings, as in ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "equation": {
                "content": "q \\rightarrow E_q = [e_{q1}, e_{q2}, \\dots, e_{qm}] ∈ \\R^{m×d}\n",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": ". Then, ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "MAX_SIM",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": " has been applied to compare the two embedding lists and obtain the final score between the query and the document page. ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "UesUdHp1Jo28nNxegWmcXxNYnyj",
        "block_type": 4,
        "heading2": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "ColBERT text retrieval system",
                "text_element_style": {
